applied   0145-kiwi-admin-resync.patch                    c40ecb47 (v1.902, feature port B.2)  FEATURE PORT (plan section B.2): wholesale re-sync of the admin-page stack to KiwiSDR v1.902 — web/kiwi/{admin.js,admin.html,w3_util.js,kiwi.css,w3_ext.css} + admin_sdr.js one-liner (id-sdr_hu→id-public; upstream tab ids are label-lowercased). 3-way merge per file vs Beagle_SDR_GPS bases (admin.js b13b4ebd, w3_util.js f80c2d0d, kiwi.css 8b58cd74, admin.html 2ae9316d, w3_ext.css a7f61ff6); 64 admin.js conflicts resolved: take v1.902 framework (admin.tabs tab builder, id-panels-container layout, new admin_confirm_* restart/reboot/poweroff scheme, Users-tab code, GNSS SBAS menu, MTU/hostname/restart_delay network widgets, log/console Copy buttons, clean-logs button) + re-apply Web-888 deltas (rx-888 branding/links, variable RX sample rates admin.c_rates, narrowband/wf_share/airband switches, WiFi mode+ssid+password, MQTT section, Update Channel Alpha/Stable, gpsd-based slim GPS tab with az/el canvas + prn_name, hotspot/ping-rx-888 console buttons, df -H / folded from 0003, #0533bd blues, w3_table_body(), web-888.51x60 logo). Server-protocol compatibility splices (Web-888 ui/admin.cpp unchanged): rev_register reverted to "SET rev_register user=.. host=.." (no reg/auto args, x3 call sites), proxy reload_url uses adm.proxy_server:admin.proxy_port, status 101 text rx-888, dropped dead kiwisdr.com sends (restart_proxy/my_kiwi_register), removed rev_auto auto-proxy UI (adm.rev_auto* absent), restored live private-proxy-server widget+cb (upstream commented out), blacklist flow reverted to clear→chunked-set→enable protocol (theirs' lock/start/disable has no server handlers; admin_recv locked case dropped), Users tab dropped from admin.tabs (no "SET get_user_list" server handler), kiwi.* compat shim (NAM/DUC/PUB/SIP/REV, hw=1, WIN_WIDTH_NOM=1465, PLATFORM_BBAI_64=2, RX8_WF3=5 — Web-888 kiwi.js lacks these), w3_restart_cb/w3_reboot_cb restored (lost in merge), admin_rx83_mode_alert stubbed (Kiwi FPGA promo, no mode tab). Known-dead cosmetic widgets (documented, future server work): SET hostname, SET ethernet_MTU, SET domain_check. 0003-state-paths.patch admin.js hunk (df -H /) folded in; 0003 shrunk accordingly. admin.html takes upstream DOM (id-panels-container) keeping Web-888 logo+rx-888 link.
          v2 (2026-08-06, post-hardware-test fix): first deployment broke the USER UI — upstream v1.902
          w3_util.js calls isNumberElse() which lives in upstream kiwi_util.js, absent from RaspSDR's
          fork (P2 audit covered kiwi.js globals but not kiwi_util.js/kiwi_ui.js helpers — lesson
          recorded in docs/dev/CHANGELOG.md). Static undefined-reference scan
          (.tmp/undef-scan.js, post-stack tree) found the full gap; patch grew to 9 files with
          verbatim upstream helper ports, each marked "// Web-888: ported verbatim from KiwiSDR
          v1.902 (B.2 admin re-sync dep)":
          - kiwi/kiwi_util.js: isEmptyString, isNumberElse, kiwi_isOld_iOS,
            any_modifier_key_except_shift, kiwi_array_iter_dup, kiwi_array_join_cond, kiwi_dhms,
            kiwi_sort_ignore_case, kiwi_sort_numeric, kiwi_storeDelete/Read/Write (kiwi.noLocalStorage
            undefined here => localStorage path, correct default), isdigit/isalpha/isalnum/islower,
            kiwi_remove_escape_sequences.
          - kiwi/kiwi.js: kiwi_output_chars (upstream console-c2w path escapes < >; RaspSDR's didn't).
          - kiwi/kiwi_ui.js: sd_done (Backup/SD status; upstream placement).
          - kiwi/admin_sdr.js: config_init + dx_html_init (upstream placement; called by admin.js
            sdr_mode branch), admin.reg_status.* → admin.status.* (x4 sites; upstream v1.902 renamed
            the field and admin_sdr.js follows upstream there).
          - kiwi/admin.js: control_confirm_show() alias → admin_confirm_show() in the shim block
            (RaspSDR admin_sdr.js dx-convert confirm still uses the pre-v1.902 name).
          ant_switch_admin_msg left unguarded upstream-style (Web-888 server never sends antsw_*;
          dead path). Patch regenerated by per-file diff -u against a post-series-minus-0145 base
          (0126 touches admin_sdr.js, 0122/0144 touch kiwi.js — diffing vs pristine HEAD would fold
          those series changes into 0145; first regen attempt caught this via slot-apply failure).
          Re-verified: slot application byte-identical, node --check all 6 JS files, undef-scan clean
          (remaining hits = function params / isFunction-guarded ant_switch / browser Highlight API).
          v3 (2026-08-06, admin-page live test): two ant_switch-extension coupling fixes.
          Web-888's admin page never loads the extension JS (upstream loads it via
          extint_load_extension_configs), so upstream's bare references broke:
          (1) init case called ant_switch_config_html() bare -> ReferenceError killed
          the rest of init; changed to w3_call('ant_switch_config_html') (silent no-op
          when absent, kiwi idiom). (2) status_interval's `if (ant_sw && ...)`
          ReferenceErrored every second; added `var ant_sw;` declaration in the shim
          block (a bare var never overwrites a later-loaded real declaration).
          Cosmetic-only, left as upstream: px(NaN) trace from admin_draw ->
          init_panel_toggle (identical call at upstream admin.js:5056); dropped
          ant_switch_nch case is not a regression (extension JS absent means the old
          w3_call was a no-op too; server message now falls to ADMIN UNKNOWN log).
          v4 (2026-08-06, user-page live test): control panel rendered as a 15px
          sliver at bottom-right. Root cause: v1.902 w3_util.js INSERTED a `navbar`
          argument into w3_nav/w3_navdef/w3_click_nav (old sig: next_id first) and
          turned w3_fillText's trailing args into an opts object. RaspSDR's
          openwebrx.js (optbar navbar) and ext.js still call the old signatures;
          with v1.902 code the anchor ids come out wrong and w3_click_nav silently
          returns (w3_el(nav_id) null), so optbar_focus never fires and the panel
          keeps its index.html height:0. Full arity-diff audit of old-vs-new
          w3_util.js: only these 4 functions are breaking (the rest appended
          optional trailing args). Fix: compat dispatch in w3_util.js — new-style
          detected by "id-" prefix on the nav argument; legacy bodies kept verbatim
          as w3int_anchor_legacy/w3_nav_legacy/w3_navdef_legacy/w3_click_nav_legacy;
          w3_fillText old-style (font string as arg6) mapped to opts object.
          Verified live pre-fix: #id-control inline height 0px -> 15px; manual
          optbar_focus() restored 228px.
applied   0146-webcpp-restore-ext-list-js.patch            follow-up to 0144                  BUGFIX (0144 regression): 0144's web.cpp brought upstream's "#ifdef USE_SDR" guard around the EXT_LIST_JS iparams registration, but Web-888's cmake build never defines USE_SDR (Kiwi Makefile concept) -> EXT_LIST_JS was never registered, so admin.html served the literal %[EXT_LIST_JS] token and extension JS (ant_switch etc.) stopped loading on the admin page. Pre-dates B.2 (existed since 0144's deploy; invisible because RaspSDR's old admin.js never referenced extension globals). Patch removes the guard with a Web-888 comment. Restores pre-0144 behavior: %[EXT_LIST_JS] substitutes <script>/<link> tags for every registered extension on the admin page. Applies after 0145 in the series (web.cpp untouched by 0145, so diff base is identical either way).
0145  | NOTE v5: w3_util.js shim restructured after live admin-page "too much recursion" --
        the original `var w3_nav_v1902 = w3_nav;` capture-at-append-time silently captured the
        hoisted DISPATCHER itself (function declarations hoist script-wide, so the appended
        redefinitions replaced the originals before the var assignments ran) -> new-style
        calls recursed forever, blanking /admin. v5 renames the four original v1.902
        definitions in place (w3_nav_v1902 / w3_navdef_v1902 / w3_click_nav_v1902 /
        w3_fillText_v1902 at their definition sites) and drops the var captures; dispatchers
        now reference the renamed originals directly.
applied   0147-kiwi-fax-recording-info-leak.patch           f98b3779 (post-v1.902)           SECURITY/info-leak cherry-pick: removes the FAX extension's server-side recording — every FAX received by any user was written to a fixed, world-downloadable file /root/samples/fax.chN.pgm (DIR_DATA) that anyone could fetch afterwards, leaking other users' receptions. Upstream replaced recording with a browser-side Save button that exports the displayed canvas as a timestamped JPEG download (like the other extensions). Removes FaxDecoder FileOpen/FileWrite/FileClose (+pgm plumbing), fax.cpp's SET fax_file_open/close handlers (incl. pgmtoppm/ppmtogif non_blocking_cmd_system_child) and serno[], FAX.js's record icon/fax_download_avail handling in favor of fax_save_cb (canvas.toDataURL -> kiwi_timestamp_filename('FAX.', '.jpg')). Fork adaptations: no .min.js/.gz shipped (upstream hunks N/A); hand-applied around pre-existing fork tweaks (4-channel SND_RATE ProcessSamples signature, per-bandwidth init, w3-ext-retain-input-focus sfmt, HF FAX layout). //fax_file_cb(0,0,0) commented trace kept, matching upstream post-fix. FaxDecoder.cpp hunk #2 applies with fuzz 2 (context-only drift); dry-run verified against pristine pin tree.
applied   0148-mongoose-epollerr-graceful-close.patch       none (Web-888 local fix)          LOCAL FIX (not a cherry-pick): epoll EPOLLERR in mg_iotest() (the "socket error 2" log/drop observed on /admin ~0.5 s after connect) now reads SO_ERROR via getsockopt() first — only a real pending socket error takes the mg_error hard-close path; a clean SO_ERROR (graceful peer close, e.g. admin browser navigating away) is treated as readable/HUP so the normal read path closes the connection quietly. Precedent: pkgs/sdrpp_server/sdrpp_server.cpp SO_ERROR check. Scope: epoll branch only; poll/select "socket error 3/4" paths keep upstream behavior (Web-888 builds MG_ENABLE_EPOLL). Background + root-cause trace: docs/dev/mongoose-websocket-socket-error-investigation.md. Applies after 0144/0147 (mongoose.cpp untouched by 0014-0017, position-independent); dry-run verified against the post-0147 series tree. Operator opt-in given 2026-08-11; QEMU + hardware smoke gate owed before release.
